editorialMd:
The working idea

The input contains exactly two sorted drawers. Produce all their readings in one sorted sequence, preserving duplicates.

Return the smallest value in the derived sequence, or 0 for an empty sequence.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n); space O(n).

javascript
function pairedDrawersFloorTicket(drawers, k) {
  const a=drawers; let out=[];
  let i=0,j=0;while(i<a[0].length||j<a[1].length){if(j===a[1].length||(i<a[0].length&&a[0][i]<=a[1][j]))out.push(a[0][i++]);else out.push(a[1][j++]);}
  return out.length?Math.min(...out):0;
}


